### Why

`LearningResponse` (`pattern.ts:779-782`) carries three ACE 1.5 done-event fields: `cumulative_v15_reward_delta?: number`, `patterns_rewarded?: number`, `reward_tier?: string`. These are returned in the SSE `done` event payload and in the non-streaming `/traces` response.

Neither `src/tools/aceLearn.ts` nor `src/chat/commands/learn.ts` read or display these fields. `aceLearn.ts:82` accesses `result.learning_statistics` for pattern counts, but never checks `result.cumulative_v15_reward_delta` or `result.reward_tier`.

Displaying these gives the AI immediate confirmation that the reward model updated — a UX signal that the F-080 loop closed successfully.

---

### What

**File: `src/tools/aceLearn.ts`**

```ts
// BEFORE — output block (lines 77-119) — no reward fields shown
let output = `✅ **[ACE] Learning captured!**\n\n`;
// ... shows stats.patterns_created, stats.patterns_updated etc.

// AFTER — append reward signal after the stats block
if (result.reward_tier || result.cumulative_v15_reward_delta !== undefined) {
    output += `\n🏅 **Reward:** `;
    if (result.reward_tier) {
        output += `${result.reward_tier} tier`;
    }
    if (result.cumulative_v15_reward_delta !== undefined) {
        const sign = result.cumulative_v15_reward_delta >= 0 ? '+' : '';
        output += ` (${sign}${result.cumulative_v15_reward_delta.toFixed(2)} delta)`;
    }
    if (result.patterns_rewarded) {
        output += ` · ${result.patterns_rewarded} patterns rewarded`;
    }
    output += `\n`;
}
```

Apply the same addition to `src/chat/commands/learn.ts` after the statistics block.

